 "source": "MikroElektronika LCD mini Click v101 (MIKROE-2453): 2D and 3D files (LCD_mini_Click_2d_3d_files.zip: CAD/lcd mini click v101.dxf, LCD mini click v101.step), schematic v101. Part centres from the STEP's placements and the DXF pads (U1's STEP origin is its pin 1; its body is centred in its silkscreen box), body sizes from the packages (SOIC-28W, SOIC-8, SOT-23, 0603, 0805). PWR SEL drawn on 3.3V, the schematic's. The display (Topway LMB162XFW, 53 x 20 mm, LMB162XFW manual 1.2) hangs on a 16-way ribbon from CN1; here it lies over the Click, turned so its text reads upright on today's boards (both hold Clicks turned 90 degrees) and kept inside the room a slot has (the art is 60.4 mm long). Its bezel (43.5 x 19.3), glass (36.4 x 10.1, the model's 296 x 82 frame), backlight end blocks and corner holes are measured from MikroElektronika's product photo (7.245 px/mm on the 53 mm PCB); the ribbon and CN1's exact body are not drawn (CN1 from its silkscreen box).",
